    pr_ref:  # e67d
    description: "Analogue check for WI-juzaj. Neither Ruby (Gemfile / Gemfile.lock) nor PHP (composer.json / composer.lock) feeds a DependencyManifest, so Ruby and PHP boundary nodes get no directness stamp. Both need a name rule from the code reference to the package: Ruby require paths -> gem names (require 'active_support/core_ext' -> activesupport; not 1:1, needs a conservative rule + Gemfile.lock specs), PHP namespaces -> composer packages (composer.lock autoload psr-4 prefixes give an exact namespace->package map, preferable to any heuristic). Mirror mix_deps.py / npm_deps.py: scoped tables in DependencyManifest.scoped, a resolver in supply_chain._SCHEME_RESOLVERS, a LANGUAGE_PACKAGE_SCHEME entry, unmatched -> no stamp."  # e67d
    fields: {}  # e67d
